ok - keyed blockers retain worker summaries and resume only after every blocker clears
ok - keyed declared waits emit waiting and resume when resolved
ok - paused keys survive drains and repeated or unsolicited status declarations do not emit
ok - configured wait vocabulary uses the same lifecycle transitions
ok - pure readers and captain-hold mirror rows never emit lifecycle events
ok - a discarded cursor rebuilds history silently and emits only new bytes
ok - absent hook leaves the status classifier unchanged
ok - successful teardown emits finished with the retired task context
